{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463957-self-embrace-question","id":463957,"title":"Self-Embrace Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T15:49:07-07:00","id":463957,"title":"Self-Embrace Question","content":"Anyway, due to a weird confluence of events, I've decided one of my living BBEGs' particular method of immortality (trading away humans to the True Fae for youth and years of luck) is slowly turning him into a vampire; every time dies and is reborn, he develops a trait more akin to one of the Kindred until eventually he'll come back without a heartbeat and a need for blood (I explicitly call it selling so much of his humanity that a Beast filled the vacuum).<br /> <br /> Thing is, I'm not sure what clan he'd be. He's a Civil War-era slaver with skills in voodoo (he particularly enjoys a zombification spell to create perfect servants), so Ventrue isn't unlikely (particularly given that one voodoo bloodline), but given the fact there are minor clans in Blood and Smoke, you think he could be the progenitor of a new one? What Banes and Disciplines would it have?<br /> <br /> Also, I think it would be fitting if he was born a Neglatu-because it'd be ironic (he is and remains the slaver, but he can never truly be safe from his slaves rebelling, because Neglatu can't form blood bonds).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T16:14:36-07:00","id":463978,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would be tempted to give him a unique Clan or at least Bloodline. My suggestions in short:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Unique Clan (TBN)</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Celerity, Dominate, Obfuscate<br /> Celerity feels to me to be the most &quot;fae&quot; of physical Disciplines. Obfuscate also feels fae (there are some parallels to a Changeling's Mask even). Dominate fits his nature and past.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane (Idea #1)</b>: The ??? Curse. As he has robbed in life, so he will forever in death. Everytime he feeds from a willing vessel (this includes regular blood dolls and NPCs covered by the Herd merit, but not vessels coerced through Disciplines) he gains no nourishment from it and instead takes 10 - Humanity points of Bashing Damage. Freely given blood will never nourish him.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane (Idea #2)</b>: The Fae Curse. Being attacked with an object made of Cold Iron deals an additional 10 - Humanity points of Bashing damage to him. Furthermore, he has to keep any promises he makes. When he fails to adhere to a promise or oath, he takes 10 - Humanity points of Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane (Idea #3)</b>: The Decorous Curse. He is unable to reject a gift freely given, even if this puts him into peril. Rejecting any gift or friendly act requires a Willpower point and all his dicepools are capped by Humanity for the rest of the night.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a Bloodline I would make him Ventrue or Mekhet. Give him Dominate as a Mekhet or Obfuscate as a Ventrue. For Bloodline Bane I would suggest using one of the above with the following modifications:<br /> <br /> <b>Bane 1</b>: Straight 5 points of damage<br /> <b>Bane 2</b>: An additional 2 points of damage (Cold Iron)<br /> <b>Bane 3</b>: Remove the Humanity cap afterwards<br /> <br /> <br /> As a Clan/Bloodline Merit, maybe something that grants him Vitae for making fae deals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T16:35:38-07:00","id":463981,"title":"","content":"Saibot's suggestions are excellent. I'll echo that I wouldn't feel constrained by the existing clans, and would feel totally comfortable &quot;making one up&quot; for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T06:54:33-07:00","id":464638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463957-self-embrace-question#post463957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, due to a weird confluence of events, I've decided one of my living BBEGs' particular method of immortality (trading away humans to the True Fae for youth and years of luck) is slowly turning him into a vampire; every time dies and is reborn, he develops a trait more akin to one of the Kindred until eventually he'll come back without a heartbeat and a need for blood (I explicitly call it selling so much of his humanity that a Beast filled the vacuum).<br /> <br /> Thing is, I'm not sure what clan he'd be. He's a Civil War-era slaver with skills in voodoo (he particularly enjoys a zombification spell to create perfect servants), so Ventrue isn't unlikely (particularly given that one voodoo bloodline), but given the fact there are minor clans in Blood and Smoke, you think he could be the progenitor of a new one? What Banes and Disciplines would it have?<br /> <br /> Also, I think it would be fitting if he was born a Neglatu-because it'd be ironic (he is and remains the slaver, but he can never truly be safe from his slaves rebelling, because Neglatu can't form blood bonds).</div> </div> </div> </div>More info please on BBEG. What Skills or attributes does he favor? Based on the scant info I don't see the Lord connection. <br /> <br /> Mekhet maybe? <br /> <br /> Maybe Nos?<br /> Think about it. Not quite right due to being fae touched. Trading folk to inhuman beings to be slaves could be monsterous. And Nightmare can be seen as a form of dark glamour.<br /> Banes: Something built around Rowan, Arithmania (which is common to vamps and fae), stopped by red brick dust (voo doo), Promiscuous bane( he has a high chance of accidentally creating larvae (zombies)when he feeds and kills, xtra points if they can track him like revenants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T08:37:42-07:00","id":464701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463957-self-embrace-question?p=463978#post463978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would be tempted to give him a unique Clan or at least Bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Disciplines</b>: Celerity, Dominate, Obfuscate<br /> Celerity feels to me to be the most &quot;fae&quot; of physical Disciplines. Obfuscate also feels fae (there are some parallels to a Changeling's Mask even). Dominate fits his nature and past. </div> </div> </div>I also concur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bane (Idea #2)</b>: The Fae Curse. Being attacked with an object made of Cold Iron deals an additional 10 - Humanity points of Bashing damage to him. Furthermore, he has to keep any promises he makes. When he fails to adhere to a promise or oath, he takes 10 - Humanity points of Bashing damage. </div> </div> </div>I'd favour this out of Saibot's bane suggestions, though my own suggestion would be to use only the iron vulnerability (cold iron is just a poetic add-on, though it should be pure rather than any old steel) and make the damage lethal.<br /> <br /> The lack of blood bonds would also make a good bane, perhaps as a counterpart to Dominate: he can make slaves, but only with effort and micromanagement; the easy way of making and keeping is beyond him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:27:06-07:00","id":464920,"title":"","content":"When talking about how each of the clans have a different origin, how they're each were a different kind of supernatural before they mutated into a vampire? Ventrue are the ones closest to the fae with their history and personality. I'd just go with them as the &quot;fae lord&quot; type","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:33:50-07:00","id":465233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463957-self-embrace-question?p=464638#post464638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More info please on BBEG. What Skills or attributes does he favor? Based on the scant info I don't see the Lord connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I intend for him to be very emblematic of the evils of slavery and the social systems that create it; he's a classic Southern Gentleman (you know, white suit, folksy accent, polite, and oozing upper class) and thinks of himself as such; he was only recently reborn into the modern world, and his schemes are driven by a need to reclaim his &quot;proper place&quot;, his wealth, prestige, and hopefully land. Thing is, he's reached the point where &quot;racist&quot; isn't really the proper term-he's such a <i>classist </i>that anyone nearing the poverty line is less than human to him, African-Americans not the least of them (though he's prejudiced against the ethnicity he used to buy and sell too, they're in the &quot;ill-bred impovrished scum&quot; category until proven otherwise-and even with rich examples he's going to assume they somehow lucked into it or have white backers). Transitioning to buying and selling slaves to the True Fae was just a lateral step for him-they're just fellow slave owners, if otherworldly ones, to him.<br /> <br /> That's where the Lord idea comes from.<br /> <br /> I agree with Sunless Nick's vote at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T19:17:51-07:00","id":506329,"title":"","content":"Reviving this thread on something I just realized:<br /> <br /> What <i>Covenant </i>is he?<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone works, as does Invictus, but the Sanctified seem like people he'd get along with most easily, given his life and the fact he made the switch from immortality to undeath fairly recently. Also emphasizes his fundamental link to a very dark part of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:33:44-07:00","id":506434,"title":"","content":"Somewhat paradoxically (given that they're kind of all about embracing their monstrousness), the Sanctified might not be a good fit if he doesn't feel any guilt or regret regarding the choices he made in life. The Sanctified teach that only unrepentant sinners become vampires (&quot;The evil become Damned; God has taken those worthy of His love to His own side.&quot;), and this is presumably particularly true of one who wasn't deliberately embraced. They'd likely tell him that his condition was a consequence of his pridefulness and for consorting with what were clearly demonic beings. If that sounds like something he'd strongly disagree with, they may be a bad fit.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul, on the other hand, may be quite interested in the unique circumstances of his embrace, as well as the means by which he had previously attained living immorality. They'd probably welcome him, and encourage him to keep in touch with the Fae, in order to hopefully glean some useful secrets from them. If he's hoping to in some way reverse his transformation into a one of the kindred, or at least reduce the impact of his new vulnerabilities and urges, he might well be inclined to take the Dragons up on their offer.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone might work, if the local Crone cult models itself on Voodoo to some degree. That's assuming, of course, that he's a practitioner of the Voodoo religion, rather than merely someone who picked up some sorcerous tricks originating in the Voodoo tradition. There's more to being an Acolyte than just casting spells, after all, and it would be a bit odd for a southern &quot;gentleman&quot; to also be a blood-drenched goddess-worshiper (though the contrast might be interesting).<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Invictus seems like the most natural fit, given the way you've characterized the man. They're likely to care far less about his unusual origin than about the resources he can contribute to the covenant. Just remember, though, that as a newcomer to kindred politics he's going to have to be willing to take orders from his elders if he wants to fit in with the First Estate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-07-2015, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T01:22:12-07:00","id":506521,"title":"","content":"The strange way he became a Vampire reminded me of the strange way Jiang Shi became vampires. In a way they turn them self in to vampires what is quit similar to this fellow. So I think I would make him a Jiang Shi.<br /> <br /> The Circle is for sure the most obvious choice for the covenant (because of Voodoo!). As such a special kind of individual I think it would be justified to make him either unaligned or gave him Membership in two Covenants, maybe Circle and Invictus, or Circle and Ordo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T06:46:32-07:00","id":507999,"title":"","content":"I agree with the 'own clan' idea, and Neglatu sounds like a good fit. Another idea is to go with a translated clan from masquerade, possibly Cappadocians, or Kissad if you want to keep a fae theme, but that might as well be 'make your own clan'.<br /> <br /> Also, he's a Hudoon? If not, you'll want to explain how he knows Hoodoo and what the Loa think of him.<br /> <br /> Covenant wise, he can be an independent, but that depends on what the elders of your city think of slavery. The more who look down on it or compare it to the blood bond (maybe they were bonded in their youth) the more likely this is. I agree that the Lancea et Sanctum doesn't sound like his deal, and as CatDoom says, the Invictus sound like the best fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:00:31-07:00","id":511873,"title":"","content":"The whole zombie-slaves thing tempts me to make him as some sort of riff on VtR's Burakumin or VtM's Cappadocians &amp; Giovanni, but that is just me toying with ideas and images, no particular idea so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T22:47:31-07:00","id":529612,"title":"","content":"Making him is own 'clan' and discipline and bane spread is great.<br /> <br /> I would say covenant wise his choices really are unaligned, CotC and OD.<br /> <br /> If the Invictus found out he was not embraced but became a vampire by falling in league with beings the Invictus are unable to act against but can act against the Invictus (in theory and vamps are super paranoid), the Invictus would see him as a potential spy and kill him just to be safe. Not to mention, if he can only feed on unwilling chattle that's a security risk in Invictus eyes. People build herds to make feeding less time consuming and reduce Masqurade breaches.<br /> <br /> If the LS found out and believed him, they'd probably label him sort of Belial/CotC abomination and kill him. <br /> <br /> The Crone would be very interested in him for obvious reasons and so would the OD. Personally I think he would go OD or join the Invictus and secretly be OD. While the Invictus are a good fit for him, if your guy is that motivated to aquire and successfully achieved immortality, he's not going to stop there. Why settle with his currently limitations when he can potentially achieve a more refined and powerful state of immortality with the OD? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}